  assign comp_search_blobs = 'prime minister’s spelling bee writing spelling a national kids’ spelling tradition. three reading levels (green years 3-4, orange 5-6, red 7-8). kids compete from school, with state finalists progressing to a national final. past winners have met the actual prime minister. spelling national|crikey! magazine photography competition (australia zoo) photography & film run by australia zoo and the irwin family. big-ticket prizes: 2 nights at the crocodile hunter lodge (over $1,800 value), australia zoo family passes, signed gift baskets. robert irwin started his photography career here as a junior finalist. photography,environment national|national water week poster competition social good run by water authorities like yarra valley water and greater western water. the 2026 theme is ’water heroes: make every drop count.’ posters can be drawing, painting, mixed media or digital. category winners progress to statewide finals during national water week (19-25 october). art,environment national (state water authorities)|book links short story writing competition writing a nice low-key one for upper primary writers. $100 prize plus the winning story published on the book links website. open theme. writing national|acmf national songwriting competition performance run by the australian children’s music foundation. over $20,000 in prizes - all paid towards musical equipment or tuition (so prize money goes straight back into music). a breakthrough comp for any kid who writes songs in their bedroom. music national|nunga kids art competition art flagship run by the commissioner for aboriginal children and young people in sa. a safe, celebrated space for first nations kids to express themselves through creative artwork on the year’s national aboriginal and torres strait islander children’s day theme. all artwork displayed at the commissioner’s office during naidoc week. art,culture sa|save the frogs! art contest art international frog conservation through art. junior (under 18) and student categories. aussie kids welcome. quirky, niche, surprisingly popular. art,environment international|national schools poster competition (nspc) social good project-based learning meets statistics, sustainability and stem. kids design and run their own investigation, then create a digital poster to share what they found. cash prizes per division ($15-$40 individual). optional second stream specifically for sustainability investigations. science,stem,environment national|asme young composers awards (state-based) performance state-by-state competition for young composers. multiple categories - solo instrument, ensemble, choir, rock/pop/edm with or without lyrics. winning compositions are performed live at the awards ceremony. music sa, qld, others|australian cartoonists association prize (in theinmag) art in the mag going since 1924, the aca picks a winner from the cartoons kids send in to theinmag each issue. no separate entry form. the winner gets a year of inkspot, their own magazine, plus a chance to meet australia’s best cartoonists. art national|camp australia big art comp art brand-led australia’s biggest oshc provider runs a national art comp every single term. hundreds of kids enter each round. past prizes have included custom hoodies featuring kids’ own artwork, lego creative happy boxes, $50 art shed vouchers, and a grand prize trophy designed by the brickman himself. real artist kerry evitts judges each round. art national|crayola creative acts of color (open call) art brand-led crayola’s ’creative acts of color’ is an open call rather than a traditional comp - kids share their creative work on social tagged @crayola and #staycreative. less about winning, more about being part of a global creative movement. crayola also runs an annual crayola creativity week (typically january). art international|state premier’s reading challenges writing reading not a competition - a challenge. hundreds of thousands of kids do this each year. read enough books from your state’s curated booklist and earn a certificate signed by the premier. the vibe is participation, not winning - but it’s a big motivating force for reluctant readers. each state runs its own version with similar mechanics. reading nsw, qld, vic, wa, sa, tas|flickerfest flickerup (australian national youth competition) photography & film australia’s leading short film festival - and the academy award qualifying one. the youth competition (flickerup) screens at bondi alongside the international films. winning here is a proper foot in the door of the aussie film industry. film national|international festival of owls kids’ art contest art international started in 2004 as a small us festival comp, now over 2,000 entries from dozens of countries. niche but enthusiastic - a perfect home for kids who love owls (and kids who love owls really love owls). no ai, no adult help. original art, posted to minnesota. art international (postal to usa)|apsmo maths olympiad (years 5-6) stem designed for kids who light up at hard maths problems. running since 1987. four contests, 5 questions each, no calculator. less about the answer, more about how creatively you got there. maths,stem national (and nz)|children’s rights queensland art competition art civic run by children’s rights queensland in partnership with the queensland family and child commission. 2025 theme was ’every queensland child is loved, respected and has their rights upheld.’ over 300 entries received in 2025, with first/second/third place winners sharing $2,000+ in prizes across age groups. art,culture qld|class clowns performance run by the melbourne international comedy festival. a free workshop with a professional comedian, then perform at a real heat in front of a live audience. past participants include joel creasey and rhys nicholson. cash prize $1,500 for the national grand final winner plus $1,000 for their school. comedy,performance national|eckersley’s art & craft prize art brand-led launched 2025 to celebrate eckersley’s 60th anniversary. national exhibition at hazelhurst arts centre in september. while the headline prize targets adult artists, this one’s worth tracking for any youth/junior categories that may be added. art national|eckersley’s kids colouring competition art brand-led eckersley’s art & craft is australia’s beloved 60-year-old art supplies chain. kids pick up a free colouring sheet at any eckersley’s store (or download it online), colour it in any way they like - pencils, paints, crayons, anything goes - and submit. winners scoop $50 eckersley’s gift cards. art national|faber-castell create your mark art brand-led a whole-class crowd-pleaser. faber-castell partners with cool australia to build a curriculum-aligned brief for aussie classrooms - kids create using faber-castell products around themes like ’create your mark for a brighter future.’ the school of the most inspiring entries scores $1,500 worth of faber-castell products. art national|first lego league (australia) stem where kids fall in love with engineering. teams research a real-world problem, build a lego robot to solve missions, and present their solutions at competitions that escalate from regional to national to international. coding,stem national (and global)|micador brand giveaways art brand-led aussie owned art supplies brand. micador runs regular brand giveaways - ’win a year of micador,’ ’win a year of early start,’ etc. sub-brands include early start (toddlers), micador jr. (kids), micador (tweens) and micador for artists. art national|nsw children’s week art competition art civic run by the nsw advocate for children and young people. the 2025 theme was ’everyone should know about children’s rights’ based on article 42 of the un convention on the rights of the child. group entries allowed and encouraged. three age categories with 1st, 2nd and 3rd place per category. art,culture nsw|oz schools instrumental championships (osic) performance a national series of state championships culminating in a national final. kids qualify by audition, nomination, or by placing 1st-3rd in an australian eisteddfod. top placers go to state finals at iconic venues. music national|smiggle christmas card competition art brand-led the cult aussie kids’ stationery brand runs an annual christmas card design comp. kids download a template, draw the front cover, colour it in - the winning design gets featured on actual smiggle christmas cards. prizes typically include vouchers and smiggle gear. art national|staedtler secondary school artist of the year art brand-led staedtler runs an annual high-school comp with a $5,000 prize pool. weekly random draw of $200 staedtler art packs throughout the entry period. plus a people’s choice voting round. three professional australian artists judge. art national|staedtler world kids colouring day art brand-led a global initiative by staedtler that’s been running for 18 years. kids submit a drawing on the year’s theme, and for every picture submitted staedtler donates to a plan international project supporting girls’ education - in 2026 this funds education for girls in malawi. art national (international)|very short film festival - junior category (vsff) photography & film australia’s coolest under-the-radar youth film festival. selected films premiere at the vsff festival weekend in hobart, then tour nationally. the festival publishes a free step-by-step filmmaking guide. phone footage is fine. film national|wakakirri national story-dance festival performance australia’s largest performing arts event for schools - over 10,000 students annually since 1992. schools tell a story through dance, drama and music. the 2026 theme is ’guardians of us.’ performed in professional theatres, with regional video options. less about technical dance, more about creative storytelling. performance,dance national|just write - for kids (sa public libraries) writing run by marion city council’s library network. first prize up to $200, second up to $100. word limits 300-750 (9-10s) or 500-1,000 (11-13s). open theme. writing sa|sydney royal easter show - junior arts & crafts art royal show australia’s biggest creativity showcase has been running since 1869 - approximately 5,500 exhibits across 500 categories. the junior art, craft & design competition has hundreds of classes for kids aged 2-20. winning entries displayed in the arts & crafts pavilion, the third-most-visited pavilion at the easter show. art national (nsw)|young archie art flagship the little sibling of the archibald, australia’s most prestigious portrait prize. kids paint, draw or pastel a portrait of someone who matters to them - a parent, a grandparent, a best friend - and finalists hang in the art gallery of nsw alongside the grown-ups. art national|think science! competition (ansto) stem run by ansto (australia’s nuclear science and technology organisation). free entry, generous prizes for winning schools. designed to teach science inquiry skills in a fun way. particularly strong at primary level. science,stem national|cossack children’s art awards art flagship a regional wa gem. each child gets a free 30x30cm canvas to paint, and finalists are exhibited at the galbraith store in cossack alongside the famous cossack art awards. category winners receive $100, the overall winner takes home $300 plus a 50% framing discount. plus art packs from paintbox for highly commendeds. art wa - regional only|dorothea mackellar poetry awards writing one of australia’s longest-running and most prestigious kids’ poetry comps, named after the woman who wrote ’my country.’ 2026’s optional theme is the traveller. cash prizes plus an annual anthology that publishes winners, runners-up, shortlisted and commended poems. entries can be solo, group, or whole-class. no ai. writing,poetry national|nsw premier’s spelling bee writing spelling the classic spoken spelling bee. kids compete at class level, then school level, then regional level via video. winners progress to state finals at penrith performing & visual arts. spelling nsw|nsw writeon competition writing the annual creative writing comp run by the nsw department of education in partnership with the state library. the 2026 stimulus: ’it was a small thing, but it made a difference.’ winning entries are published in the ’best of writeon’ anthology - a real book, kids’ words in print. writing nsw|spencil art prize art brand-led run by aussie kids’ stationery brand spencil. major prize packs worth $400 each plus 20 runner-up prizes and weekly staff picks. the prize pack includes get arty colouring sets, silky crayons, art smock, sketchbook and more - so the prize itself is fuel for the next masterpiece. art national|the golden pen (scribblers festival) writing run by scribblers festival, perth’s kids’ lit festival. the 2026 theme is metamorphosis. overall winner gets an e-reader and book pack ($249 value). shortlisted entrants get 6-month book subscriptions. bonus: classroom entries of 5+ can win a workshop with a scribblers creative. writing,poetry wa|cya conference hatchlings award writing run by the cya conference (children’s & young adults’ writers conference). solid cash prizes - $100 first, $60 second, $40 third. categories vary by writing form, with word counts to match. writing national|little sydney lives photography competition photography & film run by city of sydney as part of the australian life program. kids capture sydney through their own lens - phone snaps welcome, no fancy gear needed. from harbour sparkle to suburban stillness. selected works exhibit outdoors in central sydney. photography nsw (sydney)|randolph stow young writers award writing cash prizes for primary writers in regional wa. winners get a perpetual trophy displayed in their school until end of term 2 the following year. two students from years 6-11 also win passes to the literature centre’s young writers collective program. writing,poetry wa - regional only|shaun tan award for young artists art flagship named after picture book legend shaun tan (the arrival, the lost thing). winners’ work hangs in a month-long public exhibition at subiaco library, professionally framed or mounted. the city of subiaco picks up the framing tab. no ai-generated work allowed. art wa|whitsunday voices short story competition writing cash prizes for first, second and third place in each age category. word limits step up with year level - 300-400 for grades 3-4, up to 1,200 for years 11-12. pure creative freedom on subject matter. strictly no ai. writing national|australian museum ocean photography (young ocean photographer) photography & film linked to the australian museum’s ocean photographer of the year program. three winners receive om system tough tg-7 underwater cameras - actual gear they can use to take more photos. photography,environment national|big science competition (asi) stem run by australian science innovations. 50 minutes, mixed format, problem-solving and critical thinking in real-life contexts. pathway to the australian science olympiads program. science,stem national (and international)|laura literary awards (prose & poetry) writing run by the rocky river writers club out of country sa. a lovely small-but-mighty comp with two streams - prose and poetry (cj dennis poetry awards). $25 to junior winners, $15 to junior primary. note: entries must be posted, not emailed. writing,poetry national|south perth young writers award (spywa) writing shortlisted entrants score a one-on-one workshop with a published local author for tailored feedback. finalists get prizes up to $150 and have their work published in a spywa anthology - one copy gifted to each finalist, one to their school library, one held in city of south perth libraries. writing wa - regional only|whitlam institute what matters? writing competition writing a really special one. the whitlam institute asks kids one question - what matters? - and lets them answer however t